<title>JAPAN: Calsonic to invest $45 mln in Mexico plant.</title>
<headline>Calsonic to invest $45 mln in Mexico plant.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calsonic Corp said on Wednesday it would invest $45 million to build a car parts plant in the industrial region of San Francisco, Aguas Calientes in northern Mexico.</p>
<p>Calsonic will produce radiators, air conditioners, and silencers at the plant which is due to start operations by late 1998, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The automobile parts will be supplied to Nissan Motor Co Ltd's unit in the United States, for its &quot;Sentra&quot; model cars, he said.</p>
<p>Calsonic is 33.4 percent owned by Nissan.</p>
<p>The production capacity of the planned plant was not available.</p>
</text>
